# Vendored third-party code, checked in byte-for-byte.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows rewrites line endings on checkout, which would change these
# files' digests — and a digest that no longer matches the published tarball is a vendored
# file nobody can verify. `-text` tells git to leave them exactly as committed.
#
# Scoped to this one directory on purpose. The repository has no line-ending policy of its own
# and this is not the commit to invent one in; every other path keeps whatever behaviour it
# has today.
apps/web/public/vendor/** -text
